    <string name="title_one_call_version_help">Which One Call version?</string>
    <string name="content_one_call_version_help">OpenWeatherMap serves forecasts through its One Call API, in two versions giving the same data. They differ only in the keys they accept.\n\n3.0 works with keys subscribed to the “One Call by Call” plan. It is free up to 1,000 calls a day, but OpenWeatherMap asks for a bank card to subscribe. Set a limit of 1,000 calls a day in your OpenWeatherMap account and you will never be charged.\n\n2.5 is the former version, closed to keys created from June 2024. Some older keys still work with it, without a subscription.\n\nIf your key is refused, try the other version.</string>
